 "wears": [],
 "guns": {
  "about": "The RPG-7V as a gun a game fires (core's guns3d, through item3d's sidecar): its words for each stage it brings, its points and where a hand takes each part in each clip. Every point is in the kit's frame (x the launcher's right, y toward the muzzle, z up, metres, the launcher's zero as rpg7.py's header says), on the bone whose name ends with `bone` when a part carries it, else on the launcher itself; `turn` is degrees about the item's own x, y and z (y up, the muzzle toward -z) of the hand that takes it. Each clip of `hands` gives each hand that moves in it a list of [seconds, point]: the hand on that point at that moment, moving straight from each to the next; `rest` is where each hand is when no clip of `hands` plays. `left hand` and `right hand` are the empties a body's hands reach for, which guns3d moves along `hands` every frame; they stand where `rest` puts them as the gun is made.",
  "words": {
   "trigger": {
    "select": {
